The live loop updates. To do a deterministic test, I can drive the test purely through the live loop: set up the scenario, then sample the player state over real frames using rAF in the page, collecting the minimum vLong after contact and the position delta.

Let me write a test script.

Plan in page:
```js
await window.__apex.demoRace(0,{instant:true});
// wait for race
window.__apex.startRaceNow();
// position player 6m behind AI 0
const r = window.__apex.race;
const a = r.ai[0];
// place AI ahead with speed
...
```
To place the player behind the AI along the track: use a.dist and sample. We don't have sampleAtDistance exposed. But we can position using the AI's model position and rotation: player.position = AI pos - forward*6. And set yaw = AI yaw, vel = forward*45. AI speed = 25.

Then record:
- min vLong
- max backward displacement along the forward axis relative to the starting point.

Sample over ~1.5s with rAF, then resolve.

Also record whether contact happened (distance approaches ~2m). And check vLong stays > 0.

Careful: with the AI at speed 25 and the player at 45, the auto-drive may brake. We can set input.gas = true to force throttle 1. Player steering input 0.

Let's write the test in /tmp/opencode.

